# Rust Codebase Rules
# See full rules in RULES.md and .cursor/rules/rust.mdc

- Hard limits: <400 lines/file (fail), <60 lines/fn (fail), 8-10 fns/file, <=4 params/fn, nesting <=3.
- Zero tolerance: no dead code, no #[allow(...)] without single-line // reason:, no unwrap/expect outside tests/main boundary.
- Zero warnings: cargo build and clippy must pass with 0 warnings.
- Architecture: domain/ never imports infra/ or api/. infra/ implements domain/ traits.
- Tests: unit tests colocated in cfg(test) mod tests, integration tests in tests/.
